---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const terms = [
  { term: "BRIMJOB", def: "When Pretty Mouth Boy does something good as Brimstone. The squad types it in chat. He has never asked them to stop.", color: "#f5a623" },
  { term: "SITE ADJACENT", def: "Good Chill Night's signature positioning philosophy. Near the site. Not ON the site. Close enough to hear the bomb plant. Too far to do anything about it.", color: "#f5d623" },
  { term: "CRASHOUT", def: "A meme that TJC sent so many times in the group chat that it became a way of life. Used as a greeting, farewell, battle cry, and existential statement. CRASHOUTCRASHOUTCRASHOUTCRASHOUT.", color: "#17ecc2" },
  { term: "THE GAMING CHAIR THEORY", def: "Scientifically proven phenomenon where Doodlleus's gaming chair loses all power at exactly 11:00pm. Before 11pm: cracked aim, clutch plays. After 11pm: a man desperately trying to stay awake. The chair knows.", color: "#c742f5" },
  { term: "SPLOINK?", def: "One of Doodlleus's many cryptic one-word messages used to initiate game night. Others include: Oingoboingo? Chimchimcheroo? Boom boom pow? Boing? Doink? Moo? The squad always knows what it means.", color: "#c742f5" },
  { term: "AYE", def: "Neilatron's universal response to any question about playing Valorant. Sometimes followed by falling asleep before the lobby loads.", color: "#7aff4a" },
  { term: "PURCHANCE", def: "Pretty Mouth Boy's way of saying 'yes.' Not 'perchance.' Purchance. It's deliberate. Probably.", color: "#f5a623" },
  { term: "MAYB / MAYHAPS / MEBE3", def: "Good Chill Night's spectrum of noncommittal responses. All translate to 'yes but I need 10 minutes.' She always shows up.", color: "#f5d623" },
  { term: "I COULD DO EXACTLY ONE", def: "TJC's legendary commitment level. Will play exactly one game. Unless the squad wins, in which case, one more. Unless they lose, in which case, revenge game. Somehow plays 4.", color: "#17ecc2" },
  { term: "VALORANT OS", def: "TJC's dedicated operating system partition exclusively for Valorant. He dual-boots into it for game nights. This is either extremely dedicated or extremely unhinged.", color: "#17ecc2" },
  { term: "THE FACTORIO META", def: "Pretty Mouth Boy's strategy of dying first in Valorant so he can alt-tab to Factorio. Exposed by TJC: 'Jack dies first so he can play Factorio.' Confirmed by Pretty Mouth Boy himself: 'I'm tired and want to play Factorio on my main screen.'", color: "#f5a623" },
  { term: "IM UP FOR LOSING SOME RR", def: "Neilatron's go-to acceptance message for game night invites. It is both a prediction and a promise. The RR will be lost. The vibes will remain.", color: "#7aff4a" },
  { term: "THIS IS WHY IM THE VIPER", def: "What TJC says after every Viper play, regardless of whether the play was actually good. Misses a snake bite by a full tile? 'This is why im the viper.'", color: "#17ecc2" },
  { term: "THE ODIN PROTOCOL", def: "The squad's unofficial strategy of buying Odins just to watch the enemy team complain in all chat. Is it optimal? No. Is it funny? Every single time.", color: "#ff4655" },
  { term: "THE ACE WATCH", def: "The ongoing, possibly eternal, vigil for Good Chill Night's first ace. When told tonight could be the night, she replied: 'Look me in the eyes and tell me you believe that.' The squad looked away.", color: "#f5d623" },
  { term: "NOT A GAMER ANYMORE", def: "What Pretty Mouth Boy says before playing 4 games in a row. It has never been true. He is always a gamer. He just doesn't want to admit it.", color: "#f5a623" },
  { term: "THE BAIT REZ", def: "TJC's signature Sage move. Teammate dies in the open? TJC rezzes them right there. No smoke. No wall. Just vibes. Survival rate: roughly 12%.", color: "#17ecc2" },
  { term: "HEALING GOES AGAINST EVERYTHING SHE BELIEVES IN", def: "The squad's assessment of Good Chill Night when she was suggested to play Sage. She does not heal. She does not rez. She does not nurture. She places a turret and waits.", color: "#f5d623" },
  { term: "TEAM GUN GAME", def: "The squad's custom game mode. Everyone must get a kill with the current gun before the team moves to the next one. Knife kill at any point skips the current gun. The order: Pistol > Stinger > Bulldog > Marshal > Spectre > Guardian > Outlaw > Operator > Bucky > Phantom > Ares > Judge > Vandal > Odin > Knife. The Lotus 4-knife round is the peak of human achievement.", color: "#ff4655" },
  { term: "THE LOTUS INCIDENT", def: "4 knife kills in a single round on Lotus during Team Gun Game. The greatest moment in squad history. Nothing before or since has come close. If you weren't there, you wouldn't understand. If you were there, you still don't understand how it happened.", color: "#ff4655" },
  { term: "FUCK YOU GOOD CHILL NIGHT", def: "Doodlleus's catchphrase. Used after good rounds, bad rounds, aces, deaths, wins, losses, and loading screens. It is not targeted. It is not personal. It is simply the natural state of Doodlleus. Good Chill Night has never once asked him to stop, which the squad interprets as consent.", color: "#c742f5" },
  { term: "WASTELAND VANDAL", def: "TJC's Vandal skin of choice. Unironically. In 2026. The squad has staged multiple interventions. He will not change it. The Wasteland Vandal looks like it was found in a skip and TJC treats it like a family heirloom.", color: "#17ecc2" },
  { term: "I THOUGHT WE WERE SAVING", def: "Said every single force round. The squad agrees to save. Four people force buy. The one person who actually saved gets destroyed with a Classic while the rest of the team dies with Vandals they couldn't afford. Next round, someone forces alone, has no money for three rounds, and says 'I thought we were forcing.' The economy is a suggestion. Nobody follows it.", color: "#ff4655" },
  { term: "DEFUSE", def: "What Good Chill Night shouts when the squad is attacking. Not defending. Attacking. There is no bomb to defuse. The squad is planting. She knows this. She does it anyway. Every single time. It has caused at least three people to briefly hesitate mid-round. She has never apologised.", color: "#f5d623" },
  { term: "THE MINIMAP", def: "A feature of Valorant that Doodlleus refuses to acknowledge exists. The minimap shows enemy positions, teammate locations, and utility placement. Doodlleus uses none of this information. He plays Valorant like it's a horror game — everything is a surprise. The squad has pointed at the minimap. They have pinged the minimap. They have screamed about the minimap. He does not look at it. He will never look at it.", color: "#c742f5" },
];
---

<Layout title="THE GLOSSARY // tHeRe's nO WaY We lOsE ThIs™">
  <section class="glossary-hero">
    <div class="hero-overlay"></div>
    <div class="hero-content">
      <a href="/" class="back-link">&larr; BACK TO BASE</a>
      <span class="section-tag">// SQUAD INTEL</span>
      <h1>THE GLOSSARY</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">A FIELD GUIDE TO OUR VOCABULARY</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="glossary-list">
    {terms.map((t, i) => (
      <div class="term-card" style={`--accent: ${t.color}; --i: ${i}`}>
        <div class="term-index">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</div>
        <div class="term-content">
          <h2 class="term-name">{t.term}</h2>
          <p class="term-def">{t.def}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    ))}
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .glossary-hero {
    position: relative;
    padding: 10rem 4rem 4rem;
    background: var(--val-darker);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .hero-overlay {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse at 20% 50%, rgba(255,70,85,0.08) 0%, transparent 60%);
  }

  .hero-content {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    color: var(--val-cream);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 3px;
    opacity: 0.5;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    transition: all 0.3s;
  }

  .back-link:hover { opacity: 1; color: var(--val-red); }

  .section-tag {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 4px;
    color: var(--val-red);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .glossary-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 6px;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .hero-sub {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    letter-spacing: 4px;
    opacity: 0.4;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .glossary-list {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 2rem 8rem;
  }

  .term-card {
    display: flex;
    gap: 2rem;
    padding: 2rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(236,232,225,0.05);
    transition: all 0.3s;
  }

  .term-card:hover {
    padding-left: 1rem;
    background: rgba(236,232,225,0.02);
  }

  .term-index {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 700;
    opacity: 0.5;
    min-width: 2rem;
    padding-top: 0.3rem;
  }

  .term-name {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 4px;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    text-shadow: 0 0 20px color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 20%, transparent);
  }

  .term-def {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    opacity: 0.65;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .glossary-hero { padding: 8rem 1.5rem 3rem; }
    .glossary-list { padding: 2rem 1.5rem 6rem; }
    .term-card { gap: 1rem; }
  }
</style>
